     In order to determine the even extent of heat distributing in the rectangular pan
exactly, it is necessary to separate the outer edge of the rectangular pan to several
sections evenly. Then discretize the temperatures of each section, and obtain their
variance. So the temperature variance of pan’s outer edge could be satisfied for
describing the even extent of heat distribution. The lesser the variance is, the better
the even extent will be. As a result one obtains:
